🔹 1. Transfer Backend Files to EC2
scp -i /path/to/key.pem -r /local/backend docker-compose.yml ubuntu@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>:~/


Use: Copies backend files from your local system to the EC2 server securely using SSH.

🔹 2. Connect to EC2 Server
ssh -i /path/to/key.pem ubuntu@<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>


Use: Logs into the EC2 instance remotely.

🔹 3. Start Docker Containers
docker-compose up --build -d


Use: Builds and starts Django + MongoDB containers in background mode.

🔹 4. Stop Docker Containers
docker-compose down


Use: Stops and removes running containers.

🔹 5. View Backend Logs
docker-compose logs -f backend


Use: Shows real-time logs of the Django backend container.

🔹 6. Build React Frontend
REACT_APP_API_URL=http://<EC2_PUBLIC_IP>:8000 npm run build


Use: Creates optimized production build of React app and sets backend API URL.

🔹 7. Remove Public Access Block from S3
aws s3api put-public-access-block --bucket <bucket-name> --public-access-block-configuration "BlockPublicAcls=false,IgnorePublicAcls=false,BlockPublicPolicy=false,RestrictPublicBuckets=false" --region us-east-1


Use: Allows the S3 bucket to become publicly accessible.

🔹 8. Add Public Read Policy to S3
aws s3api put-bucket-policy --bucket <bucket-name> --policy '<policy-json>' --region us-east-1


Use: Grants public permission to read website files from S3.

🔹 9. Enable Static Website Hosting
aws s3 website s3://<bucket-name> --index-document index.html --error-document index.html --region us-east-1


Use: Configures S3 bucket to host a static website.

🔹 10. Upload Frontend to S3
aws s3 sync build/ s3://<bucket-name> --delete --region us-east-1


Use: Uploads React build files to S3 and removes old files.

🔹 11. Create ECR Repository
aws ecr create-repository --repository-name earth-backend --region us-east-1


Use: Creates a private Docker image repository in AWS ECR.

🔹 12. Authenticate Docker to ECR
aws ecr get-login-password --region us-east-1 | docker login --username AWS --password-stdin <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com


Use: Logs Docker into AWS ECR to allow image push.

🔹 13. Tag Docker Image
docker tag ubuntu_backend:latest <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/earth-backend:latest


Use: Renames local Docker image to match ECR repository format.

🔹 14. Push Image to ECR
docker push <account-id>.dkr.ecr.us-east-1.amazonaws.com/earth-backend:latest


Use: Uploads Docker image to AWS ECR.

🔹 15. Install CloudWatch Agent
wget https://amazoncloudwatch-agent.s3.amazonaws.com/ubuntu/amd64/latest/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb
sudo dpkg -i -E ./amazon-cloudwatch-agent.deb


Use: Downloads and installs CloudWatch monitoring agent.

🔹 16. Start CloudWatch Agent
sudo /opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/bin/amazon-cloudwatch-agent-ctl -a fetch-config -m ec2 -s -c file:/opt/aws/amazon-cloudwatch-agent/etc/amazon-cloudwatch-agent.json


Use: Starts CloudWatch agent with custom configuration.

🔹 17. Enter MongoDB Container
docker exec -it earth_mongo mongosh


Use: Opens MongoDB shell inside running Docker container.

🔹 18. Switch Database
use intern_db


Use: Selects the application database.

🔹 19. View Users Collection
db.user.find().pretty()


Use: Displays all user documents in formatted view.

🔹 20. View Tasks Collection
db.task.find().pretty()


Use: Displays all task documents in formatted view.

🔹 21. Exit MongoDB Shell
exit


Use: Closes MongoDB shell.
